<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Minamoto no Yoshitsune</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1159">1159</a>–<a href="/years/1189">1189</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Minamoto no Yoshitsune was a Japanese general, younger half-brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoritomo">Minamoto no Yoritomo</a>, whose victories at Ichi-no-Tani, Yashima and Dan-no-ura in 1184–1185 destroyed the Taira clan in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genpei-war">Genpei War</a>. After falling out with Yoritomo he fled to the Northern Fujiwara at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiraizumi">Hiraizumi</a>, where he was attacked by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujiwara-no-yasuhira">Fujiwara no Yasuhira</a> and killed himself in 1189. He became one of the great tragic heroes of Japanese legend and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoshitsune.jpg" alt="Minamoto no Yoshitsune" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Minamoto_no_Yoshitsune.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
